WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:08.920
Billions of years ago, water flowed on Mars. Rivers built deltas, like this one in Jezero crater.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:11.800
Where did all that water and air go?

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:22.830
Since 2014, NASA's MAVEN orbiter has measured how the Sun strips gas from the top of the Martian atmosphere.

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:29.520
Without a global magnetic shield, the solar wind carried much of the air away over time.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:35.530
To warm Mars, we would need a much thicker atmosphere.

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:46.460
In 2018, a NASA-supported study added up all the carbon dioxide we could release. It would bring the pressure to only a few percent of Earth's.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:51.850
Not enough. With today's technology, Mars cannot be terraformed.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:01:03.240
Earth's air presses about a thousand millibars. Mars today: about six. All the reachable carbon dioxide: about twenty.

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:06.570
Some dreams take more than one lifetime.

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:12.580
<v Goicochea>Paulet started with an engine. We will leave the next chapter to you.

